-- title:
--   Stalkwise principal ideal sheaves are invertible
-- statement:
--   Let $X$ be a locally Noetherian scheme and let $I$ be a quasi-coherent ideal sheaf datum on $X$, so that $I$ assigns to each affine open $U$ of $X$ an ideal $I.\mathrm{ideal}\,U \subseteq \Gamma(X,U)$ compatibly. Assume that for every point $x \in X$ there exist an affine open $U \subseteq X$ with $x \in U$ and a section $g \in \Gamma(X,U)$ such that $g$ lies in $I.\mathrm{ideal}\,U$, the image of $I.\mathrm{ideal}\,U$ in the localisation of $\Gamma(X,U)$ at the prime ideal of $\Gamma(X,U)$ corresponding to $x$ under the affine identification $U \cong \operatorname{Spec}\Gamma(X,U)$ is the principal ideal generated by the image of $g$, and the image of $g$ in that local ring is a non-zero-divisor. The conclusion is that $I$ satisfies `IsInvertible`: for every $x \in X$ there are an affine open $U$ of $X$ and $f \in \Gamma(X,U)$ with $x \in X.\mathrm{basicOpen}\,f$, together with a non-zero-divisor $g$ of $\Gamma(X, X.\mathrm{affineBasicOpen}\,f)$ such that $I.\mathrm{ideal}\,(X.\mathrm{affineBasicOpen}\,f)$ is the ideal generated by $g$.
--
--   This is the standard local criterion identifying the invertible (effective Cartier) ideal sheaves on a locally Noetherian scheme: principality by a non-zero-divisor in each local ring already holds on a basic open neighbourhood, by Noetherianity of the relevant ideal and of the annihilator of the local generator. It is used in the construction of effective Cartier divisors on modular curves, where invertibility of a kernel ideal sheaf is verified at the level of local rings.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicGeometry_Scheme_IdealSheafData_isInvertible_of_forall_exists_map_ideal_eq_span_singleton_of_mem_nonZeroDivisors.lean

